7.	(1) That the total taxes payable by any taxpayer under the normal rate of tax and the graduated rates of tax shall be reduced by the amount paid by the taxpayer in respect of
(a)	payments into any approved superannuation, retirement or pension fund or plan, paid as a term of employment and not repayable during the continuance of such employment;
(b)	premiums on life insurance policies in force prior to the twenty-third day of June, 1942;
(c)	principal payments on a mortgage on one residential property*, provided such mortgage was registered and in effect prior to the twenty-third day of June, 1942;
Provided, however, that such reductions shall not exceed the amount of the refundable portion of the tax as provided for in resolution 6 above; and the said refundable portion shall be reduced accordingly;
(2) That in the case of a taxpayer over sixty-five years of age with income less than three thousand dollars, the total taxes payable under the normal rate of tax and the graduated rates of tax shall be reduced by the refundable portion of the tax as provided for in resolution 6 above, and the said refundable portion shall be eliminated accordingly.
